<section class="section section-soft"><div class="shell recognition-grid"><div><h2 class="section-title">The missed opportunity may already be in the business.</h2></div><div class="recognition-copy"><p>Picture a week where the team has worked hard, but a good lead still hasn’t heard back. A customer who used to reorder has gone quiet. The numbers exist somewhere, but pulling them together takes another afternoon.</p><p>It’s easy to jump from that frustration to “we need better software.” Sometimes you do. Sometimes the first fix is much smaller.</p><p>I spent years building software with business owners at Upstack Studio. Now I’m building Second Team. I use that experience to help you assess the work involved and whether the business would benefit.</p><a class="text-link" href="/client-stories/">Client feedback from my agency years{{ icon("arrow", "link-arrow") }}</a></div></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="shell content-grid"><h2>Is this a fit?</h2><div class="content-body"><h3>You have customers, a team and a problem worth fixing.</h3><p>The best fit is usually a founder-led B2B company with about USD $1M–$20M+ in yearly revenue, 10–200 people and an existing customer base. It is an especially good fit when customers buy more than once and follow-up is inconsistent.</p><p>You can bring the relevant business data and explain how the work happens today. We use that to work out what deserves attention.</p><div class="boundary">We start with your business problem and assess whether AI would help.</div></div></div></section>
